<title>USA: NYMEX adds new delivery point for Alberta futures.</title>
<headline>NYMEX adds new delivery point for Alberta futures.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Mercantile Exchange said it added Carbon to the list of designated interconnects with Nova Gas Transmission that may be used for delivery of Alberta natural gas futures if buyer and seller agree.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the contract, which will be launched Friday, gas is based on delivery on the Nova Gas Transmission pipeline system or, if the parties agree, at designated interconnects with Nova, which already include facilities operated by Alberta Energy Co and CrossAlta Gas Storage.</p>
<p>Carbon is owned by Canadian Western Natural Gas Co Ltd and operated by CU Gas Ltd.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk 212-859-1624</p>
